---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Rycode — Working Notes & Systems Journal">
  <div class="writing-layout">
    
    <!-- ===========================================================
         FEATURED WRITING CANVAS / LEAD ESSAY
         =========================================================== -->
    <article class="lead-article" aria-labelledby="leadHeading">
      <header class="lead-header">
        <span class="lead-topic-tag">Working Paper · Systems Architecture</span>
        <h1 class="lead-title" id="leadHeading">
          The Architecture of Modern Systems: Models, Inference, and Governance
        </h1>
        <p class="lead-subtitle">
          Notes on structuring intelligence, high-stakes operational risk, and the emerging economics of autonomous software.
        </p>
        <div class="lead-meta">
          <span>By Jeff Ryan</span>
          <span>·</span>
          <span>Draft in Progress</span>
          <span>·</span>
          <span>Read Measure: 8 min</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="prose-canvas">
        <p class="dropcap">
          Building systems in an era of rapid technological inflection requires a return to first principles. Whether evaluating the mechanical limits of semiconductor packaging, calculating the total cost of ownership across sovereign infrastructure, or designing enterprise risk frameworks, clarity emerges from rigorous decomposition rather than aggregated assumptions.
        </p>

        <p>
          As machine intelligence models transition from empirical novelty to core infrastructure, the bottlenecks are shifting rapidly. We are moving from parameter scale to inference throughput, from monolithic compute clusters to localized energy constraints, and from seat-based software licensing to agentic workflows.
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          “The true constraint on technological leverage is rarely the availability of compute—it is the precision with which we define, evaluate, and contain operational blast radiuses.”
        </blockquote>

        <h2>I. The Three Core Pillars Under Deliberation</h2>
        <p>
          While rethinking the broader architecture of this platform, research and technical writing naturally converge around three core disciplines:
        </p>

        <h3>1. Frontier Intelligence & Physical Infrastructure</h3>
        <p>
          Evaluating the raw physics of compute: from advanced wafer fabrication and sub-byte quantization (NVFP4/FP8) to high-density power walls and small modular reactors (SMRs). Understanding what it actually takes to run models at scale without falling for hype cycles.
        </p>

        <h3>2. Governance, Risk & High-Stakes Containment</h3>
        <p>
          Quantifying residual risk in interconnected ecosystems. Developing models that measure control effectiveness, identify single points of failure across supply chains, and treat software governance with the rigor of safety-critical engineering.
        </p>

        <h3>3. The Inversion of Software Economics</h3>
        <p>
          Analyzing the structural shift as autonomous code generation and localized models displace conventional per-seat SaaS models, altering corporate balance sheets and vendor relationships.
        </p>

        <div class="editorial-note">
          <strong>Editor's Note:</strong> This document is an active writing canvas. Use the scratchpad below or edit this template directly in the codebase to structure upcoming essays, briefings, and system models.
        </div>

        <h2>II. Working Hypotheses</h2>
        <p>
          Technology platforms succeed when they prioritize functional transparency over cosmetic complexity. Over the coming iterations, this publication will focus on standalone, rigorous dispatches paired with interactive tools designed to verify models rather than merely present opinions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- ===========================================================
         IN-BROWSER PERSISTENT SCRATCHPAD / OUTLINER
         =========================================================== -->
    <section class="scratchpad-box" aria-labelledby="scratchpadTitle">
      <div class="scratchpad-header">
        <h2 class="scratchpad-title" id="scratchpadTitle">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M12 20h9"></path>
            <path d="M16.5 3.5a2.121 2.121 0 0 1 3 3L7 19l-4 1 1-4L16.5 3.5z"></path>
          </svg>
          Editorial Scratchpad & Outline Canvas
        </h2>
        <span class="scratchpad-status" id="saveStatus">Auto-saved locally</span>
      </div>

      <textarea 
        id="scratchpadArea" 
        class="scratchpad-textarea" 
        placeholder="Jot down notes, article outlines, structural ideas, or paste drafts here... Changes are automatically preserved in your browser's local storage."
        rows="8"
      ></textarea>

      <div class="scratchpad-actions">
        <button id="copyBtn" class="btn-secondary" type="button">Copy to Clipboard</button>
        <button id="clearBtn" class="btn-secondary" type="button">Clear Scratchpad</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===========================================================
         WORKING DRAFTS & THEMATIC DISPATCHES
         =========================================================== -->
    <section class="drafts-section" aria-labelledby="draftsHeading">
      <div class="section-divider-header">
        <span class="section-label" id="draftsHeading">Upcoming Dossiers & Themes</span>
        <span class="section-label" style="color: var(--text-faint);">In Active Development</span>
      </div>

      <div class="drafts-grid">
        <!-- Card 1 -->
        <article class="draft-card">
          <div>
            <span class="draft-status-pill">Drafting</span>
            <h3 class="draft-title">Inference Engineering & Quantization</h3>
            <p class="draft-excerpt">
              Deconstructing sub-byte precision, memory bandwidth limits, and KV-cache compression economics for low-latency serving.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="draft-meta">
            <span>Theme: AI Systems</span>
            <span>Outline Stage</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Card 2 -->
        <article class="draft-card">
          <div>
            <span class="draft-status-pill">Drafting</span>
            <h3 class="draft-title">Enterprise Risk & SaaS Blast Radiuses</h3>
            <p class="draft-excerpt">
              Mathematical modeling of internal control effectiveness, supply chain concentrations, and dependency failure modes.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="draft-meta">
            <span>Theme: Governance</span>
            <span>Outline Stage</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Card 3 -->
        <article class="draft-card">
          <div>
            <span class="draft-status-pill">Drafting</span>
            <h3 class="draft-title">The Datacenter Power Wall</h3>
            <p class="draft-excerpt">
              Investigating gigawatt interconnect queues, behind-the-meter nuclear deployments, and thermal management architectures.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="draft-meta">
            <span>Theme: Infrastructure</span>
            <span>Outline Stage</span>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    // In-browser scratchpad persistence
    const STORAGE_KEY = 'rycode_editorial_scratchpad_v1';
    const textarea = document.getElementById('scratchpadArea');
    const statusEl = document.getElementById('saveStatus');
    const copyBtn = document.getElementById('copyBtn');
    const clearBtn = document.getElementById('clearBtn');

    if (textarea) {
      // Load saved draft
      const saved = localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);
      if (saved) {
        textarea.value = saved;
      }

      // Auto-save on input
      textarea.addEventListener('input', () => {
        localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, textarea.value);
        if (statusEl) {
          statusEl.textContent = 'Saved';
          setTimeout(() => {
            statusEl.textContent = 'Auto-saved locally';
          }, 1200);
        }
      });

      // Copy action
      copyBtn?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        if (!textarea.value) return;
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(textarea.value);
          const original = copyBtn.textContent;
          copyBtn.textContent = 'Copied!';
          setTimeout(() => { copyBtn.textContent = original; }, 1500);
        } catch (e) {
          console.error('Failed to copy', e);
        }
      });

      // Clear action
      clearBtn?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (confirm('Clear the contents of your scratchpad?')) {
          textarea.value = '';
          localStorage.removeItem(STORAGE_KEY);
          if (statusEl) statusEl.textContent = 'Cleared';
        }
      });
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
